  "narrative": "<h3 class=\"story-subheading\">Short impact summary</h3>\n<p class=\"story-text\">Aristotle and the Ontology of St. Bonaventure (2023), published by Leuven University Press, has been cited 2 times. Beyond that, it has been downloaded 2,098 times.</p>\n<h3 class=\"story-subheading\">Full narrative</h3>\n<p class=\"story-text\">Aristotle and the Ontology of St. Bonaventure by Franziska van Buren was published by Leuven University Press in 2023. Conceptually, the work connects to Aristotelianism, Philosophy, Ontology, Scholarship and Interpretation (philosophy).</p>\n<p class=\"story-text\">OpenAlex records 2 citations. Notable citing venues include Religions. The citing works include 1 journal article and 1 dissertation. The citing authors are based in the United States.</p>\n<p class=\"story-text\">It has been downloaded 2,098 times via OAPEN. Its subject matter aligns with Quality Education among the Sustainable Development Goals. The work was funded by KU Leuven and European Research Council.</p>",
